invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_point.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: the conversion to Jacobian coordinates multiplies Y by Z where
  the formula multiplies it by Z^2, so every point whose Z is not 1 comes
  out as another point. bin/p256_equiv_test converts multiples of G with
  the Z the additions before left, there and back.

--- old
    p256_wide_fe_mul(&o->y, &a->y, &zz);
--- new
    p256_wide_fe_mul(&o->y, &a->y, &a->z);
